Z||000017||Ken Wittlief||12-21-2001||03:12 PM||||add also has a flip side to it - HyperFocusing<P> its similar to becoming obsessed with something - like you get an idea inyour head, or you want to take up a new hobbie or project that you have never done before<P> and its all you think about and its all you do for weeks at a time - and you are able to make incredible progress and do things in weeks that take a 'normal' person a year or more.<P> Great characteristic to have if you are an entrepenour, artist, musicain...<P> and if you learn to recognize it and accept that this is 'who you are'<P> ADD is not a disability or a 'condition' - its a different way of functioning and doing stuff - some consider it a problem, others consider it a gift!||||reg||1
Z||000018||84Bill||12-21-2001||03:18 PM||||Yes Ken!<BR>Like being stubborn  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000019||Ken Wittlief||12-21-2001||10:03 PM||||being stubborn is a good thing - esp when you are right! :c)<P> BTW jeff - im willing to bet you have always had ADD<P> back when we were in school if you had ADD they told you your lazy and a slacker, and you need to apply yourself more :dO<P> now that they understand that ADD kids really do think and learn differently, the kids are doing much better in schools (even though the schools still are not 'designed' for them) Ritalin helps the kids fit into the 'program' better.<P>  I expect someday when we understand that ADD really is NOT a disorder, then there will be schools and learning programs designed for these people, and then they will really excel.||||reg||10
